<div class="card" id="getting-started">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-idea"/></svg> Getting started</h2>
  <details><summary>Is NoBossly free?</summary><p class="muted">Yes. Every path, every tool, the community, groups and cohorts are free, with no card needed.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Where do I start?</summary><p class="muted">Pick your path: creator, freelancer, coach or consultant, local service, shop or café, online store, physical product, apps and software, or still figuring it out. Then answer a few questions about where you are. It takes about a minute. Your dashboard is then set up for that kind of business.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What does my path change?</summary><p class="muted">What your dashboard puts first: the stage you're at and the next real step, the number worth tracking (billable income for a freelancer, jobs per week for a local service, takings against rent for a shop), and the boards and checklists for that work. It never locks anything away. Every tool is in your <a href="/workspace">workspace</a> whatever your path.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Can I change my path?</summary><p class="muted">Yes, any time, from <a href="/choose-path">Choose your path</a>. Your saved worksheets, boards and logs stay where they are. You can update your setup answers from <a href="/choose-path/setup">Path settings</a>.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What's in the workspace?</summary><p class="muted">Lean Canvas, Business Model Canvas, customer persona, business plan, idea refiner, elevator pitch, goals and milestones, plus the worksheets for your path, such as a proposal builder, break-even calculator or MVP scope. You'll also find your boards, number logs and checklists, a calendar of everything with a date, and the tools: Quit-Date Planner, Tax Set-Aside, Pricing &amp; Margin, Proof Page and customer interviews. Everything in it is private to you.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do surveys work?</summary><p class="muted">Build one in <a href="/surveys">Surveys</a>, publish it, and share the link. People can answer without an account. Results add up on the survey's page, and you can download them as a CSV.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Does NoBossly use AI?</summary><p class="muted">No. The tools are structured worksheets and plain arithmetic, and feedback comes from other members.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card" id="community">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-community"/></svg> The public side</h2>
  <details><summary>What's on the public side?</summary><p class="muted">Everything every member can use: the <a href="/feed">feed</a> and <a href="/community">Q&amp;A</a>, <a href="/exchange">Help &amp; exchange</a>, <a href="/reviews">feedback</a> on your work, <a href="/groups">groups</a>, collaborators, <a href="/quests">challenges and public cohorts</a>, and <a href="/wins">results</a> members share.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How does Help &amp; exchange work?</summary><p class="muted">Post an ask (what you need help with) or an offer (what you can help with), choose a category, and say whether it's free or a skill swap. Members respond, and you pick one. When it's done, the person who was helped says thanks, and that shows on the helper's profile.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Why can't I post my email or phone number?</summary><p class="muted">To keep members safe from scrapers and spam, emails, phone numbers and street addresses aren't allowed in public posts, profiles or group posts. Connect through NoBossly <a href="/messages">messages</a> instead.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What kinds of groups are there?</summary><p class="muted"><strong>Public</strong> groups: anyone can see and join. <strong>Private</strong> groups: listed, but only members see posts, and you ask to join. <strong>Hidden</strong> groups: not listed at all, and joined by invite link only. Anyone can start a group and choose which kind it is.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What are the Monday and Friday posts in groups?</summary><p class="muted">Weekly check-in threads. Every Monday at 9am New York time, each group gets "What are you working on this week?", and every Friday, "What went well this week?". Reply in the thread. Group owners and admins can turn either off in the group's settings.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What can group roles do?</summary><p class="muted">Owners and admins manage settings, invite links and roles. Moderators approve join requests and remove posts. Mentors set assignments and review work. Members post and reply.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I report something?</summary><p class="muted">Use the Report link on the post, comment or profile. Blocking someone hides their posts from you everywhere, and yours from them.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card" id="cohorts">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-team"/></svg> Cohorts and programs</h2>
  <details><summary>What is a cohort?</summary><p class="muted">A private group run by an accelerator or program. It's invite-only and never listed, and nothing in it is visible to anyone outside it: not the posts, not the members, not the work handed in.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I join my program's cohort?</summary><p class="muted">Open the invite link your program sent you while signed in, and choose Join. If it says the link has expired or been used up, ask your program for a new one.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I hand in an assignment?</summary><p class="muted">Open the assignment from your cohort's Assignments page. For a worksheet, such as your Lean Canvas, pick which of your documents to hand in. For a board, a copy of the board goes in. Some assignments ask for a written answer or a link instead.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Can my program see my workspace?</summary><p class="muted">No. When you hand something in, a copy of it as it is at that moment goes to your program team. Your workspace stays private, and later edits aren't shared unless you hand in again.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What happens after I hand something in?</summary><p class="muted">Your program team is notified. They either approve it or send it back with feedback, and you're notified either way. You can hand in a new version until it's approved.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What can my program team see about me?</summary><p class="muted">Inside the cohort: your posts and the work you hand in. On their activity page: when you joined and were last active, how many posts you made this week, and how many assignments you've handed in. They don't see your workspace, your messages, or anything you post outside the cohort.</p></details>
  <details><summary>I run a program. How do we get set up?</summary><p class="muted">Ask the NoBossly team in the <a href="/community">community forum</a> and we'll set up your organization. Your team can then create cohorts, send invite links, set assignments and review work.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card" id="account">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-setting"/></svg> Your account</h2>
  <details><summary>How do I change my email or password?</summary><p class="muted">Both can be updated in <a href="/account">Account settings</a>. Email changes require confirming a link sent to both your old and new address.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What's the difference between a public and private profile?</summary><p class="muted">Public profiles show your full profile to other members. Private profiles show only your username. Change it in Account settings.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I deactivate or delete my account?</summary><p class="muted">In Account settings. Deactivating hides your profile and signs you out, and logging back in reactivates it. Deleting schedules permanent removal after a 7-day grace period, during which you can cancel by logging back in.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card center">
  <h3>Still stuck?</h3>
  <p class="muted">Ask in the <a href="/community">community forum</a>. The team and other members are happy to help.</p>
</div>
